    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d204">

                <pb facs="0303" n="187" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg187"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.13/27.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Scholle to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 1, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The House yesterday passed Amnesty Bill for all accused or convicted of murder,
                    attempted murder or assault and battery, providing offender is a veteran of War
                    of Cuban Independence. Further, all accomplices, and those convicted of
                    newspaper libel whether veterans or not. The result of this law will be the
                    liberation of Asbert and Arias: the murderers of General Rivas, Chief of Police
                    of Habana.</p>
                <p>It is probable that the Senate will act tomorrow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Scholle</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
